		"description": "<p>You have learned the tales of the natural world and can shout them from the proverbial—or actual—mountaintops even when out of your humanoid form. You gain the following benefits:</p><ul><li><p>Your Wisdom score improves by 1, to a maximum of 20.</p></li><li><p>You can maintain a @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.3qc1rqk8rwvl8van]{Battle Hymn} or impart @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-class-features.Item.m7siz0z3rlng8h20]{Bardic Inspiration }while wild shaped.</p></li><li><p>You are proficient with the Performance skill. If you are already proficient, you gain an expertise die. You also gain a Performance skill specialty with Speaking.</p></li><li><p>You learn the following special Battle Hymn, which does not count against your battle hymns known</p><ul><li><p><strong>Chorus of Nature. </strong>The creature gains immunity to poison and disease.</p></li></ul></li></ul>",
